ruction and famine thou shalt laugh:¦layout ‚¤textÙ8Neither shalt thou be afraid of the beasts of the earth.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ9For thou shalt be in league with the stones of the field:¦layout ‚¤textÙ8And the beasts of the field shall be at peace with thee.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ:And thou shalt know that thy tabernacle shall be in peace;¦layout ‚¤textÙ7And thou shalt visit thy habitation, and shalt not sin.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ2Thou shalt know also that thy seed shall be great,¦layout ‚¤textÙ.And thine offspring as the grass of the earth.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ+Thou shalt come to thy grave in a full age,¦layout ‚¤textÙ0Like as a shock of corn cometh in in his season.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ'Lo this, we have searched it, so it is;¦layout ‚¤textÙ'Hear it, and know thou it for thy good.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse